+ * Everything a human can do against this process is a GET. The dashboard in
+ * investigations/ is a pure observer: it watches the journal over SSE, inspects
+ * evidence and exports reports. Operator control (POST /api/control/*) exists for
+ * this harness and the CLI only — the loop itself never needs a human, and it can
+ * never take external consequential actions (no such tool exists here by design).
+ *
+ * The environment (corpus, remotes, faults) is a deterministic stub standing in for
+ * Crossref / Europe PMC / publisher fetch, exactly like dev/serve.mjs stands in for
+ * the cloud relay. Same role, same rule: none of it ships. Real deployment swaps the
+ * adapters behind the same task interface; the loop, evidence model and console are
+ * untouched by that swap.
+ *
+ * Safeguards baked in (architecture §7): per-remote rate limits are awaited, not
+ * bypassed; 403/paywall -> recorded inaccessible and skipped; every write is confined
+ * to the data dir (containment-checked); budgets are hard; retries are bounded; the
+ * interpreter only ever reads stored evidence and must attach alternative
